<!--
    v1.12.0 demo — report import (SSRS/RDL).

    This definition exercises the v1.12.0 territory (ROADMAP v1.12.0, README
    roadmap item 4) in one report: SSRS/RDL report import parses the report and
    links it to its datasets, distinguishing embedded, shared, and unresolved
    datasets, preserving XML source locations where the element tags are
    locatable, and keeping parser uncertainty region- or document-scoped.

    What to observe in the "Reports" menu after Apply:

      1. The status line summarises the parse, e.g.
         "1 report · 3 datasets · 2 embedded · 1 shared · 1 unresolved".
      2. The Dataset picker lists each dataset with its source kind.
      3. Selecting an embedded dataset (StudentMaster or CourseLookup) loads
         its query into the editor and runs the normal SQL analysis.
      4. The shared dataset (SharedRollup) references an external shared
         dataset definition and has no SQL to analyse in this file.
      5. The unresolved dataset (Broken) has neither a command text nor a
         shared reference, so it cannot be linked and is reported with a
         region-scoped report_dataset_unresolved diagnostic at its own element
         span.

    The embedded dataset queries are plain T-SQL, so they also analyse cleanly
    as query structure when selected:

       SELECT StudentId, StudentName FROM dbo.Student WHERE SchoolYear = @Year
       SELECT CourseId, CourseName FROM dbo.Course

    To resolve the secondary dbo.* objects by catalogue evidence, paste this
    catalogue in the Catalogue menu and Apply, then re-run:

       dbo.Student TABLE student
       dbo.Course TABLE
       COL dbo.Student.StudentId
       COL dbo.Student.StudentName
       COL dbo.Student.SchoolYear
       COL dbo.Course.CourseId
       COL dbo.Course.CourseName

    Combined report dependency views and report export remain scheduled for
    v1.13.0.

    This demo is an illustration, not an input to the fixture-corpus metrics
    (docs/metrics-v1.12.0.json). No user input or runtime telemetry is
    collected.
-->
<Report xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/reporting/2008/01/reportdefinition" xmlns:rd="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SQLServer/reporting/reportdesigner">
  <DataSources>
    <DataSource Name="SchoolDB">
      <ConnectionProperties>
        <DataProvider>SQL</DataProvider>
        <ConnectString>Data Source=.;Initial Catalog=School;Integrated Security=true</ConnectString>
      </ConnectionProperties>
    </DataSource>
    <DataSource Name="SharedStore">
      <DataSourceReference>Shared/SharedStore</DataSourceReference>
    </DataSource>
  </DataSources>
  <DataSets>
    <DataSet Name="StudentMaster">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>SchoolDB</DataSourceName>
        <CommandText>SELECT StudentId, StudentName FROM dbo.Student WHERE SchoolYear = @Year</CommandText>
        <QueryParameters>
          <QueryParameter Name="Year">
            <Value>=Parameters!Year.Value</Value>
          </QueryParameter>
        </QueryParameters>
      </Query>
      <Fields>
        <Field Name="StudentId"><DataField>StudentId</DataField></Field>
        <Field Name="StudentName"><DataField>StudentName</DataField></Field>
      </Fields>
    </DataSet>
    <DataSet Name="CourseLookup">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>SchoolDB</DataSourceName>
        <CommandText>SELECT CourseId, CourseName FROM dbo.Course</CommandText>
      </Query>
    </DataSet>
    <DataSet Name="SharedRollup">
      <SharedDataSet>
        <SharedDataSetReference>Shared/Rollup</SharedDataSetReference>
      </SharedDataSet>
    </DataSet>
    <DataSet Name="Broken">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>SchoolDB</DataSourceName>
      </Query>
    </DataSet>
  </DataSets>
  <Body>
    <ReportItems>
      <Textbox Name="Header">
        <Value>= "Student directory"</Value>
      </Textbox>
      <Tablix Name="StudentTable">
        <TablixDataRegion>
          <DataSetName>StudentMaster</DataSetName>
        </TablixDataRegion>
      </Tablix>
    </ReportItems>
  </Body>
</Report>